<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
      Out in the wilderness, Elijah finds a broom tree.<break time="500ms"/>
      A small, scrubby bush offering thin shade against the desert sun.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He sits down beneath it.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And he prays, but it is not a prayer of hope.<break time="500ms"/>
      It is enough, he says.<break time="500ms"/>
      Now, O Lord, take away my life.<break time="1000ms"/>
      I am no better than my fathers.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He is not angry.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is finished.<break time="500ms"/>
      The kind of tired where you cannot imagine one more step.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The kind of emptiness where even faith feels like a weight too heavy to lift.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And God does not scold him.<break time="500ms"/>
      God does not lecture him about his lack of courage.<break time="500ms"/>
      God does not remind him of the fire on the mountain.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Instead, Elijah lies down and falls asleep.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then an angel touches him.<break time="500ms"/>
      Gently.<break time="500ms"/>
      Arise and eat, the angel says.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And there beside his head is a cake baked on hot stones, and a jar of water.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He eats.<break time="500ms"/>
      He drinks.<break time="500ms"/>
      And he lies down again.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God's first response to Elijah's despair is not a sermon.<break time="500ms"/>
      It is bread and water and permission to sleep.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes the most holy thing God offers is rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
